module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.EpiLocallySurjective
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.AffineQcohPushforward.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraSheafModuleFunctor.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.SectionEpiAffine.Basic

/-!
# Locally surjective morphisms of quasi-coherent algebra sheaves are surjective on sections over
an affine open

Let `X` be a scheme, `φ : A ⟶ B` a morphism of quasi-coherent sheaves of `𝒪_X`-algebras whose
underlying morphism of sheaves of commutative rings is locally surjective, and `U ⊆ X` an affine
open. Then `A(U) → B(U)` is surjective.

This is the first of the two statements that [Stacks, Tag 0817] and [Stacks, Tag 05JT] are
reduced to. The point of it is that *the image in a sheaf category is the sheafification of the
image presheaf*, so a sheaf epimorphism is only locally surjective, and the sections of an image
over an affine open are not visibly the subalgebra generated by the images of the sections. This
file says they are, over an affine open, and the reason is the quasi-compactness argument of the
proof of [Stacks, Tag 01XB].

## The route

All the cohomology is in `Stacks.SectionEpiAffine.surjective_app_of_isAffineOpen`, which is
[Stacks, Tag 01EU] fed with the Čech vanishing and the cofinality statement
`Stacks.Cohomology.AffineOpen.exists_standardCover_refines` of [Stacks, Tag 01XB]. What this
file adds is the
passage between the algebra sheaves and their underlying `𝒪_X`-modules:

1. `Stacks.RelativeSpec.AlgebraSheaf.underlyingModuleMap φ` is the morphism of underlying
   `𝒪_X`-modules, which on sections over any open *is* the morphism of sheaves of rings.
2. It is therefore locally surjective as soon as `φ.right` is, and hence an epimorphism of
   sheaves of modules by `Stacks.SheafOfModules.EpiMono.epi_of_isLocallySurjective`.
3. Quasi-coherence of `A` and `B` is, by definition, quasi-coherence of the underlying modules.
4. So sections over an affine open are surjective, and the surjective map is the one on sections
   of the sheaves of rings.

## Main results

* `Stacks.SectionEpiAffine.epi_underlyingModuleMap_of_isLocallySurjective`: a locally surjective
  morphism of algebra sheaves induces an epimorphism of underlying `𝒪_X`-modules.
* `Stacks.SectionEpiAffine.surjective_sections_of_isLocallySurjective`: **the statement above** —
  sheaf-epi implies section-epi over an affine open, for quasi-coherent algebra sheaves.
* `Stacks.SectionEpiAffine.isQuasicoherent_unitAlgebra`: `𝒪_X`, as an algebra over itself, is
  quasi-coherent.
* `Stacks.SectionEpiAffine.surjective_structureMap_of_isLocallySurjective`: the case of the
  structure morphism of a single algebra sheaf, which is the map whose finiteness properties
  `Stacks.RelativeSpec.AlgebraSheaf.IsFiniteType` and
  `Stacks.RelativeSpec.AlgebraSheaf.IsFinitePresentation` are conditions on.

## Implementation notes

**Steps 1 and 2 are definitional, and deliberately so.** The three morphisms involved — `φ.right`
between sheaves of commutative rings, `Stacks.RelativeSpec.AlgebraSheaf.ringSheafMap φ` between
sheaves of rings, and the underlying morphism of presheaves of abelian groups of
`underlyingModuleMap φ` — have the same sections, the same restriction maps and the same
functions on sections; `Stacks.RelativeSpec.AlgebraSheaf.underlyingModuleValMap_app_apply` holds
by `rfl`. `CategoryTheory.Presheaf.imageSieve` depends on a morphism only through those three
things, so the local-surjectivity hypothesis transfers by passing the `imageSieve_mem` field
across, with no rewriting, and the final surjectivity statement is read off the module-level one
the same way.

**Why the hypothesis is local surjectivity and not `Epi φ`.** An epimorphism of sheaves of
*commutative rings* need not be locally surjective — `ℤ → ℚ` already is not — so `Epi φ` in the
category of algebra sheaves is the wrong hypothesis and would make the statement false. For
sheaves of modules the two notions do agree, which is what step 2 uses.

**The structure-morphism form needs no separate argument.** A morphism of algebra sheaves out of
`Under.mk (𝟙 X.sheaf)` has `φ.right = B.hom`, so the general statement applied to
`CategoryTheory.Under.homMk B.hom` already concludes about `B.hom.hom.app (op U)`. The only extra
input is quasi-coherence of the source, and
`AlgebraSheaf.underlyingModule (Under.mk (𝟙 X.sheaf))` is *literally*
`SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf`, whose quasi-coherence is the instance
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.AffineQcohPushforward.isQuasicoherent_unit`.

**No quasi-compactness or quasi-separatedness of `X`.** As in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/SectionEpiAffine/Basic.lean`, the only quasi-compactness used is
that of the affine open `U`.

**No stacks attribute is attached**: these are inputs to [Stacks, Tag 0817] taken out of the proof
of [Stacks, Tag 01XB], not tagged statements of the source.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0817](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0817)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 05JT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05JT)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01XB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01XB)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite TopologicalSpace
open AlgebraicGeometry
open Stacks.RelativeSpec

universe u

namespace Stacks.SectionEpiAffine

variable {X : Scheme.{u}}

/-- **A locally surjective morphism of algebra sheaves induces an epimorphism of underlying
`𝒪_X`-modules.** The morphism of underlying modules has the same sections and the same functions
on sections as `φ.right`, so it has the same image sieves and is locally surjective; for sheaves
of modules that is the same thing as being an epimorphism. -/
theorem epi_underlyingModuleMap_of_isLocallySurjective {A B : AlgebraSheaf X} (φ : A ⟶ B)
    (hφ : Sheaf.IsLocallySurjective φ.right) :
    Epi (AlgebraSheaf.underlyingModuleMap φ) :=
  Stacks.SheafOfModules.EpiMono.epi_of_isLocallySurjective _ ⟨fun s => hφ.imageSieve_mem s⟩

/-- **A locally surjective morphism of quasi-coherent algebra sheaves is surjective on sections
over an affine open.** For quasi-coherent sheaves of `𝒪_X`-algebras `A` and `B`, a morphism
`φ : A ⟶ B` whose underlying morphism of sheaves of commutative rings is locally surjective, and
an affine open `U`, the ring map `A(U) → B(U)` is surjective.

This is the sheaf-epimorphism-implies-section-epimorphism statement that makes the sections of an
image sheaf over an affine open computable, and it is the `H¹`-vanishing content of
[Stacks, Tag 01XB] applied to the kernel of `φ`. -/
theorem surjective_sections_of_isLocallySurjective {A B : AlgebraSheaf X} (φ : A ⟶ B)
    (hA : A.IsQuasicoherent) (hB : B.IsQuasicoherent) (hφ : Sheaf.IsLocallySurjective φ.right)
    (U : X.Opens) (hU : IsAffineOpen U) :
    Function.Surjective (φ.right.hom.app (op U)).hom :=
  let _ := hA
  let _ := hB
  let _ := epi_underlyingModuleMap_of_isLocallySurjective φ hφ
  surjective_app_of_isAffineOpen X (AlgebraSheaf.underlyingModuleMap φ) U hU

/-- **The structure sheaf, as an algebra over itself, is quasi-coherent.** Its underlying module
is `SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf` by definition, because restricting scalars along the
identity changes nothing. -/
theorem isQuasicoherent_unitAlgebra (X : Scheme.{u}) :
    AlgebraSheaf.IsQuasicoherent (X := X) (Under.mk (𝟙 X.sheaf)) :=
  inferInstanceAs ((SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf).IsQuasicoherent)

/-- **The structure morphism of a quasi-coherent algebra sheaf, if locally surjective, is
surjective on sections over an affine open.** This is
`surjective_sections_of_isLocallySurjective` for the canonical morphism out of
`Under.mk (𝟙 X.sheaf)`, and `B.hom.hom.app (op U)` is exactly the ring map that
`Stacks.RelativeSpec.AlgebraSheaf.IsFiniteType` and
`Stacks.RelativeSpec.AlgebraSheaf.IsFinitePresentation` are conditions on. -/
theorem surjective_structureMap_of_isLocallySurjective (B : AlgebraSheaf X)
    (hB : B.IsQuasicoherent)
    (hB' : Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) B.hom.hom)
    (U : X.Opens) (hU : IsAffineOpen U) :
    Function.Surjective (B.hom.hom.app (op U)).hom :=
  surjective_sections_of_isLocallySurjective (A := Under.mk (𝟙 X.sheaf))
    (Under.homMk B.hom (by simp)) (isQuasicoherent_unitAlgebra X) hB hB' U hU

end Stacks.SectionEpiAffine

end
